div.p:
Coming to look on you, thinking you dead, (And dead almost, my liege, to think you were,) I spake unto the crown, as having sense, And thus upbraided it: The care on thee depending,
                  Hath fed upon the body of my father;
                  Therefore, thou, best of gold, art worst of gold;
                  Other, less fine in carat, is more precious,
                  Preserving life in med’cine potable. Henry IV—2d, Act IV., Sc. IV.
